WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.960
Not a day goes by without the internet nearly
shutting down completely over a breaking news

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.460
story.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.320
The most recent threat of total implosion
came on May 16th, when word got out that Warner

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.139
Bros. and director Matt Reeves were nearing
a deal with Robert Pattinson to become the

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.540
new Batman, taking over for Ben Affleck.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.860
Even though Pattinson has been in plenty of
films, most only know him from his role as

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.320
the glistening vampire Edward Cullen in the
Twilight film saga.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:29.060
So to imagine him donning the cape and cowl
in Reeves' The Batman was simply too much

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:29.760
for people.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.340
Pattinson fans, those who aren't down for
the English actor to portray the famous superhero,

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.100
and everyone in between is completely freaking
out about his reported casting.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.100
One person tweeted:

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.160
"It is official, the DCEU should be canceled.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.740
This is a HORRIBLE choice to play the character."

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.820
Someone else practically shouted into the
Twitter-sphere when Pattinson's name started

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:50.980
trending on the site:

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:56.780
"Robert Pattinson getting casted proves that
@DCComics @TheDCUniverse @warnerbros HATES

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:57.580
its fans!!!

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.100
Awful just awful!!!

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.800
I've never been so disappointed in a Batman
casting!!!

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.640
Dammit!!!"

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.160
Anger over Pattinson assuming the Bat-mantle
from Affleck got so intense that naysayers

00:01:07.179 --> 00:01:12.219
started various online petitions demanding
that Warner Bros. and Reeves replace the actor

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.219
with someone else.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.079
At the end of the day, it's unlikely that
any of the appeals will amount to much more

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.760
than extra internet noise.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.720
"And Bruce Wayne?

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.120
Why are you dressed up like Batman?"

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.680
The other side of social media couldn't be
happier about Pattinson lining up to become

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.829
the new Batman, and have some advice for those
who are criticizing the casting choice two

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:35.420
years ahead of the film's June 2021 release
date.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.090
One user posted on Twitter:

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.130
"Robert Pattinson is the PERFECT.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.000
CASTING.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.500
FOR.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.300
BATMAN."

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.600
Another fan rallying behind Pattinson pointed
to the actor's work outside of the Twilight

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:50.040
franchise as evidence that he can deliver
an incredibly powerful performance, and will

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.980
likely do the same when it comes to Bruce
Wayne in The Batman.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.859
"Robert Pattinson playing Batman sounds awesome.

00:01:55.859 --> 00:01:59.979
The man truly proved himself as a wonderful
performer in these few years and I'm certain

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.140
he'll play the part well."

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.979
A Twitter user by the name of Josh Price also
urged those skeptical about Pattinson's ability

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:10.950
to give a solid performance as Batman to check
out the actor's post-Twilight movies namely

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.120
Good Time, Cosmopolis, and The Rover.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:13.940
He wrote:

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.080
"If you're in any doubt over Robert Pattinson
being cast as Batman because you only know

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.180
him from Twilight, then please watch these
three movies.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.960
Then try to tell me he isn't an amazing choice."

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:28.980
Eisner Award-winning comic book writer and
Hugo Award-nominated novelist Saladin Ahmed

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.240
gave a tongue-in-cheek response to the uproar.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.400
In a post shared to his Twitter page, Ahmed
pointed out the irony in the fact that many

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.450
of the people mad about Pattinson portraying
Batman are apparently failing to remember

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.720
how inherently silly the costumed vigilante
really is.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:43.939
Ahmed tweeted:

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.860
"'ugh [they] picked an angsty pretty boy who
spent his early 20s pretending to be a vampire'

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.269
I have bad news for you about batman."

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:56.760
JoBlo editor-in-chief Paul Shirey had arguably
the most pragmatic reaction to all the hullabaloo:

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.890
he reminded everyone that three previous Batman
actors, Affleck, Christian Bale, and Michael

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.500
Keaton, starred in their fair share of so-so
films before they became Batman.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.280
Some of them were downright goofy.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.240
"It's showtime,"

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.040
In Shirey's eyes, people shouldn't gauge Pattinson's
acting abilities solely on Twilight, as they

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.140
wouldn't judge Affleck, Keaton, or Bale on
their wackier pre-Batman works.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:25.871
The best thing is just to withhold extreme
judgements one way or the other about Pattinson

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:30.969
succeeding Affleck as the Caped Crusader until
The Batman hits theaters in 2021.

00:03:30.969 --> 00:03:35.670
Hopefully once The Batman gets closer to its
premiere date, the Pattinson-lovers and the

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.660
Pattinson-haters can settle their differences
and a general consensus about the situation

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.680
can be established.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.240
For now, keep it civil.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.080
Remember, Gotham's watching.

